def author(course):
 course('b148','分部開挖的地層支護互制、早齡襯砌與觀測回饋~Ground-support interaction, early-age lining and observational feedback in sequential excavation',
 '分部開挖讓土岩的卸載、變形與支護成形交錯發生，最終斷面強度不能單獨說明施工期表現。本課以簡化反力曲線建立概念，再逐項檢視開挖面分割、早齡材料、仰拱閉合、收斂與防水介面。學員需用量測檢查每一個模型的邊界，將適配曲線、工程判斷及正式核准清楚區分。~Sequential excavation interleaves unloading, ground movement and support formation, so final-section strength alone cannot explain construction-stage behavior. The course begins with simplified reaction curves and then examines face subdivision, young materials, invert closure, convergence and waterproofing interfaces. Learners test each model boundary against observations and distinguish curve fitting, engineering judgment and formal authorization.',
 'Crossrail的公開論文把噴凝土襯砌與地層互制及施工序列放在同一設計問題中，並回顧一九九二年Heathrow Express試驗隧道的軟土地下施工。二〇〇九年FHWA土建手冊提供另一套工程背景，二〇一四年公開的Stepney Green論文呈現側導坑序列與量測比較。這些文獻並不支持把某個縮短步距或增加厚度當成萬用解法；本課追蹤的是每一次邊界改變如何影響可觀測的力流。~Crossrail authors treat sprayed lining, ground interaction and construction sequence as one design problem, and discuss the 1992 Heathrow Express soft-ground trial tunnel. The 2009 FHWA civil manual provides another engineering reference, while the 2014 Stepney Green paper presents side-drift sequencing with monitoring comparisons. None makes a shorter advance or thicker lining a universal solution. This course instead follows how each changed boundary alters the load path and the observations needed to test it.',
 '''地層支護曲線交點~Ground-support curve intersection||地層釋放變形時需求反力可能下降，已成形支護隨變形提供更多反力；交點代表特定簡化假設下的相容狀態。支護啟用前的位移會改變交點，兩條線並不是天然固定的材料常數。~Ground reaction demand may decrease as displacement develops, while installed support mobilizes increasing resistance. Their intersection is a compatible state under specified simplifying assumptions. Displacement before installation changes that state; neither line is a universal material constant.||假設u以mm計，pg=0.6-0.02u MPa、ps=0.01(u-10) MPa且u≥10；相等得u=23.33 mm、p=0.133 MPa，僅為線性示例。~Assume displacement u in mm, pg=0.6-0.02u MPa and ps=0.01(u-10) MPa for u≥10. Equating them gives u=23.33 mm and p=0.133 MPa, a linear illustration only.||將收斂與支護應變資料配對，檢查啟用時間、初始位移和力換算的可辨識性；比較多個初始位移假設的交點，若量測不能區分它們，須保留解的範圍，不把一個最佳擬合當成唯一真實地層。~Pair convergence and support-strain histories, checking installation time, initial movement and force conversion. Compare intersections for alternative initial displacements. If observations cannot distinguish them, retain a range of solutions rather than treating a best fit as the uniquely correct ground response.||把未觀測的先期變形設為零，會高估支護參與程度並錯估交點；即使後續曲線看似吻合，起始條件錯誤仍可能造成對施工變更的錯誤預測。~Setting unobserved pre-installation movement to zero can overstate support participation and misplace the intersection. A visually good later fit does not remove that initial-condition error or make predictions of a changed sequence reliable.||地層與支護曲線一旦相交便證明所有失效均已排除。~An intersection of ground and support curves proves every possible failure mode has been excluded.||每次比較先列出啟用位移、材料齡期與三維效應的處理方式，將模型結果交設計者連同失效模式審查，不能以曲線交點自行批准下一步開挖。~Before each comparison, list installation displacement, material age and treatment of three-dimensional effects. The designer reviews the model together with failure modes; an intersection alone cannot authorize the next excavation stage.
分部面積與暴露尺度~Subdivided area and exposure scale||分割斷面改變同時暴露的面積與形狀，卻也新增接縫和施工介面。面積減少可能有利於控制某些局部機制，但總斷面與暫時支護仍需共同受力，不能將面積比例直接當作穩定度比例。~Subdivision changes simultaneously exposed area and shape while creating joints and construction interfaces. A smaller face can help control some local mechanisms, but the complete section and temporary supports still interact. Area ratios cannot directly represent stability ratios.||假設總斷面80 m²分為30、30、20 m²三部分，最大單部面積30/80=37.5%；每次假設進尺1 m時，最大單部原位開挖30 m³。~Assume an 80 m² section divided into 30, 30 and 20 m² parts. The largest part is 30/80=37.5%; at an assumed 1 m increment its in-situ excavation is 30 m³.||將實際輪廓和階段記錄重疊，核對有無相鄰部分提前開放而使合併暴露面積變大；地質面誌與暫時支護狀態需同時保存，面積計算只用於幾何核對，穩定判讀由設計者另行完成。~Overlay surveyed profiles and stage records to check whether adjacent parts opened early and enlarged the combined exposure. Preserve geological logs and temporary-support status together. Use area calculations for geometric reconciliation; the designer separately evaluates stability and interaction.||相鄰開挖面時間重疊而未更新模型，會形成比圖面預想更大的開放區；局部掉塊或變形增加可能被錯認為偶發材料問題，實際原因卻是施工序列偏離。~Overlapping adjacent excavations without updating the model creates a larger open region than planned. Increased movement or local falls may then be misclassified as isolated material problems when the underlying issue is a departure from the intended sequence.||把斷面分成三塊就能把所有荷載與風險降為三分之一。~Dividing a section into three parts reduces every load and risk to one third.||每日圖面同時標出已開挖、已支護和已閉合區，不只標累計進尺；任何部分重疊或順序調整，都須由現場技術負責人送設計審查。~Daily drawings distinguish excavated, supported and closed regions instead of showing accumulated advance alone. Any overlap or sequence change is referred by the site technical lead for design review.
早齡受壓與強度發展~Early-age compression and strength development||新噴襯砌的強度與剛度隨齡期發展，受力開始時間可能早於材料達到長期性能。平均壓應力可檢查數量級，但彎曲、局部薄區與早齡徐變會使同一平均值對不同位置產生不同影響。~Fresh sprayed lining gains strength and stiffness with age and may carry load before reaching long-term properties. Mean compressive stress checks scale, but bending, thin zones and early creep can make an identical mean stress have different implications at different locations.||假設軸力N=300 kN/m、厚t=0.20 m，單位寬平均應力N/t=1500 kPa=1.5 MPa；若合成試驗強度2 MPa，比值為0.75，未含分項係數。~Assume axial force N=300 kN/m and thickness t=0.20 m. Unit-width mean stress N/t=1500 kPa=1.5 MPa. Against synthetic test strength 2 MPa, the ratio is 0.75 before any partial factors.||把噴築時刻、溫度、核准早齡試驗與實際受力階段連起來，確認試體是否代表現場材料及養護；比較薄區和受彎位置，不能用較晚齡期強度回填較早的受力時段，差異需材料與結構人員審核。~Link spraying time, temperature, approved early-age tests and loading stages. Check whether specimens represent placed material and curing. Examine thin and bending zones; later-age strength cannot be substituted into an earlier loading interval without review by material and structural specialists.||以二十八天強度取代初齡性能會掩蓋早期需求超過能力的時段，外表未裂也不能排除內部損傷；之後補足強度不會自動抹去既有裂縫和接縫缺陷。~Using mature strength for young lining hides intervals when demand may exceed available resistance. A crack-free surface does not exclude internal damage, and later strength gain does not automatically remove cracks or joint defects formed earlier.||材料最終強度合格便能證明所有早期受力都合格。~Acceptable final material strength proves that every earlier loading stage was acceptable.||交接表以齡期而非僅以日期配對荷載和試驗，未知早齡性能要明列；下一施工階段是否可開始，由核准的材料與結構審查流程判定。~Pair loading and tests by material age, not date alone, and explicitly list unknown early-age properties. Permission to begin the next stage follows the approved material and structural review process.
薄弱截面與偏心彎曲~Weak sections and eccentric bending||非圓斷面或不均勻荷載會使襯砌同時受壓與彎曲，厚度局部減少對彎曲應力的影響大於對平均壓應力的影響。線彈性截面分析只在未裂與適用材料假設下成立，需與真實受力機制分開。~Noncircular geometry and uneven loads produce compression and bending together. Local thinning affects bending stress more strongly than mean compression. Linear-elastic section analysis applies only under its uncracked material assumptions and must be separated from the full ground-lining mechanism.||假設每米寬N=200 kN、M=10 kN·m、t=0.25 m，σ=N/t±6M/t²=0.8±0.96 MPa，兩緣為1.76與-0.16 MPa，負值表示拉應力。~For a 1 m strip assume N=200 kN, M=10 kN·m and t=0.25 m. Stress is N/t±6M/t²=0.8±0.96 MPa: edges are 1.76 and -0.16 MPa, with negative indicating tension.||用厚度檢測與幾何掃描定位不利截面，應變計資料需校正溫度和齡期後才可換算內力；若彈性模型出現拉應力，應檢討裂縫與殘餘承載模型，不把負值直接截為零再宣稱通過。~Use thickness measurements and geometry scans to locate adverse sections. Correct strain records for temperature and age before inferring forces. If elastic analysis predicts tension, review cracking and residual resistance rather than clipping negative stress to zero and declaring success.||局部薄區在彎矩作用下先裂，原有內力分配可能重新調整；只看截面平均壓縮會忽略拉側與接縫開口，進而低估滲水和後續耐久風險。~A thin zone may crack first under bending and redistribute internal forces. Looking only at mean compression overlooks the tensile edge and joint opening, potentially understating leakage and subsequent durability concerns.||平均應力是壓縮就表示襯砌每個位置都沒有拉裂。~Compressive average stress means that no part of the lining can develop tensile cracking.||圖表分別列軸力、彎矩和兩緣應力，保留正負號定義；出現開裂可能性時交設計者決定後續驗證與模型，不能只用平均值完成驗收。~Report axial force, moment and both edge stresses separately, preserving the sign convention. When cracking is possible, the designer determines further verification and modeling; a mean value cannot close acceptance.
仰拱閉合與剛度改變~Invert closure and stiffness change||開口支護和閉合環的力流不同，仰拱接通後可增加環向約束，但接縫柔度與地層接觸仍影響實際剛度。用等效彈簧比較只展示閉合改變，不聲稱結構一定立即成為完整圓環。~Open support and a closed ring have different load paths. Invert connection can add circumferential restraint, but joint compliance and ground contact still govern effective stiffness. Equivalent springs illustrate the change without claiming that closure instantly creates a perfect circular ring.||假設同一增量荷載ΔF=600 kN，開口等效剛度20 kN/mm、閉合後60 kN/mm，位移增量分別30與10 mm；兩剛度均為教學假設。~Assume the same incremental force ΔF=600 kN. With equivalent stiffness 20 kN/mm before closure and 60 kN/mm after, displacement increments are 30 and 10 mm; both stiffnesses are teaching assumptions.||核對仰拱幾何、連接完成時間與材料齡期，將閉合前後收斂增量按相同施工事件比較；排除荷載變小或基準重設的影響，才討論剛度改變，任何等效值都須附上識別資料和不確定度。~Check invert geometry, connection completion and material age. Compare convergence increments around matching construction events before and after closure. Exclude reduced loading or reset references before attributing changes to stiffness; every inferred equivalent value needs supporting data and uncertainty.||圖面已閉合但接縫未充分傳力，會讓計算剛度高於實際；若據此移除臨時構件，變形可能重新加速，顯示幾何閉合與力學閉合並不相同。~A geometrically closed section with ineffective joints can be less stiff than assumed. Removing temporary members on that assumption may restart movement, demonstrating that geometric closure and effective structural closure are different conditions.||仰拱外形接起來就代表完整承載能力立即形成。~Connecting the visible invert geometry means that full structural capacity is immediately available.||閉合紀錄同時確認幾何、接縫、齡期和核准試驗，未完成項不以照片代替；臨時支護調整前由結構負責人確認實際傳力條件。~Closure records verify geometry, joints, age and approved tests together. Photographs do not replace unresolved checks. Before altering temporary support, the structural lead confirms the actual load-transfer conditions.
施工時間與剛度相容~Construction timing and stiffness compatibility||相同軸力作用於不同齡期材料會產生不同彈性應變，而早齡徐變使單純彈性關係更受限制。施工時間表不只是管理資料，它決定各部分材料在荷載轉移時的剛度以及可能的內力再分配。~Equal axial force produces different elastic strain in materials of different age, while early creep further limits a purely elastic relation. The construction timetable is therefore a mechanical input: it determines stiffness during load transfer and potential redistribution among components.||假設單位寬A=0.25 m²、N=300 kN，E=6 GPa時ε=N/(EA)=200微應變；E=12 GPa時為100微應變，未包含徐變與收縮。~Assume unit-width area A=0.25 m² and N=300 kN. At E=6 GPa, ε=N/(EA)=200 microstrain; at E=12 GPa it is 100 microstrain, excluding creep and shrinkage.||同步記錄噴築時間、環境溫度、材料試驗與應變計啟用時刻，核對零點是否在已受力後才設定；將彈性、溫度和時間效應分別列出，無足夠證據時不能把全部應變都換算成結構軸力。~Synchronize placement time, temperature, material tests and strain-gauge activation. Determine whether zero was established after loading had already begun. Separate elastic, thermal and time-dependent components; insufficient evidence precludes converting all measured strain directly into structural axial force.||較晚啟用的儀器漏記先期應變，與年輕材料的低剛度疊加後可能誤判荷載很小；若再忽略徐變，內力估計的方向甚至可能和真實變化不同。~Late gauge activation misses earlier strain and, combined with low young-material stiffness, can suggest falsely small loading. Ignoring creep adds further bias and may make the inferred force trend differ from the actual load-transfer history.||量到的所有應變乘最終彈性模數就是當下內力。~All measured strain multiplied by the final elastic modulus gives the current internal force.||資料交接附上儀器零點時刻及材料齡期對照表，不能補填不存在的初始讀值；模型採用的剛度與時間效應由材料、監測和設計人員共同確認。~Handover includes gauge-zero times and material-age tables without inventing missing initial readings. Material, monitoring and design specialists jointly confirm the stiffness and time effects adopted in the model.
收斂曲線與外推界線~Convergence curves and extrapolation limits||指數曲線可以摘要逐漸變慢的合成收斂，但擬合形式不會自動證明地層穩定。開挖距離、地下水和後續拆除都可能改變邊界，造成原先衰減的曲線重新加速，預測必須附帶情境。~An exponential curve can summarize synthetic convergence that slows with time, but its fitted form does not prove stability. Excavation distance, groundwater and later removals can change boundaries and restart acceleration. A forecast must therefore state the scenario under which it applies.||假設u(t)=20[1-exp(-t/5)] mm，t以day計，u(5)=12.64 mm、u(10)=17.29 mm；極限20 mm只是模型參數，非現場允收限值。~Assume u(t)=20[1-exp(-t/5)] mm with t in days. Values are u(5)=12.64 mm and u(10)=17.29 mm; the 20 mm asymptote is a model parameter, not a field acceptance limit.||用保留的後期資料而非同一擬合樣本檢查預測誤差，將開挖和支護事件標在時間軸上；若殘差有系統性趨勢，應重新審查模型邊界，不能只增加曲線平滑程度讓異常看起來消失。~Test predictions on withheld later observations rather than only the fitting sample. Mark excavation and support events on the timeline. A systematic residual trend calls for boundary review; increasing smoothing until anomalies appear to vanish is not a valid response.||將加速讀值當作離群點刪除，會讓擬合曲線看似穩定卻失去預警能力；當邊界已改變，延用舊極限值可能錯估後續變形與需要的審查。~Deleting accelerating readings as outliers can make a fitted curve look stable while removing its warning value. After boundaries change, retaining the old asymptote may misrepresent future movement and the need for engineering review.||曲線擬合出有限極限值就能證明隧道已穩定。~A fitted finite asymptote proves that the tunnel has reached a stable condition.||報告保留原始點、殘差與未參與擬合的驗證區間；外推只供情境比較，任何警戒與施工決定依核准觀測方案由負責工程師判斷。~Reports retain original points, residuals and a validation interval excluded from fitting. Extrapolation supports scenario comparison only; warning levels and construction decisions follow the approved observational plan and responsible engineer.
防水介面與壓力分布~Waterproofing interfaces and pressure distribution||地下水壓力作用於可受壓的面積，防水層負責阻隔水路而非憑空消除外部水壓。排水與封閉防水的設計邊界不同，若把排水假設移植到不排水區，襯砌受力可能被低估。~Groundwater pressure acts over the pressurized area. Waterproofing blocks water paths rather than making external pressure disappear. Drained and sealed arrangements have different boundaries; applying a drainage assumption to a sealed region can understate lining demand.||假設均勻表壓p=150 kPa作用於局部平面A=2 m²，合力F=pA=300 kN；這是假設局部均壓，非整個彎曲襯砌的總合力。~Assume uniform gauge pressure p=150 kPa on local plane area A=2 m². Resultant F=pA=300 kN applies to this idealized local patch, not the entire curved lining.||核對設計排水路徑、孔壓量測及防水接縫驗證紀錄，將滲漏位置和水頭分開記錄；乾燥表面不能證明外壓為零，堵塞或排水條件改變時需由水文與結構負責人共同審查荷載假設。~Check designed drainage paths, pore-pressure observations and waterproof-joint verification. Record leakage locations separately from head. A dry surface does not establish zero external pressure; blockage or changed drainage requires joint hydraulic and structural review of the load assumptions.||排水通道堵塞後外水壓上升，內表面卻可能暫時仍乾燥；若僅以滲漏量評估荷載，會錯把防水效果良好當成結構沒有水壓需求。~After drainage blocks, external pressure may rise while the inner surface remains dry. Assessing loading from leakage alone can mistake effective waterproofing for the absence of a water-pressure demand on the structure.||內表面沒有滴水就表示外側水壓可以忽略。~A dry inner surface means that external water pressure can be ignored.||交接同時保存防水品質和排水功能證據，明示長期維護責任；壓力邊界改變先送設計審查，不以乾燥外觀代替結構荷載確認。~Retain evidence of both waterproof quality and drainage function at handover, identifying long-term maintenance responsibility. A changed pressure boundary goes to design review; dry appearance does not replace confirmation of structural loading.
反分析的多解問題~Non-uniqueness in back-analysis||單一位移可能由較大荷載配較高剛度或較小荷載配較低剛度產生，因而不是所有參數都能由一條曲線辨識。反分析必須配合獨立地質、材料與內力量測，並報告可行參數的範圍。~The same displacement can result from larger force with higher stiffness or smaller force with lower stiffness. A single curve therefore cannot identify every parameter. Back-analysis needs independent geological, material and force evidence and should report feasible parameter ranges.||假設u=F/k=10 mm，可由F=500 kN、k=50 kN/mm，也可由F=1000 kN、k=100 kN/mm得到；一個位移觀測無法區分兩組。~An observed u=F/k=10 mm can arise from F=500 kN with k=50 kN/mm or F=1000 kN with k=100 kN/mm. One displacement observation cannot distinguish the two pairs.||先列出未知參數與獨立觀測數，再用不同參數組計算是否同樣符合位移；加入有物理意義的試驗約束而非任意縮小範圍，保留同樣可行的解，交設計者評估對後續序列的預測分歧。~List unknown parameters and independent observations, then test whether several parameter sets fit the displacement equally well. Add physically supported test constraints rather than arbitrary narrow bounds. Retain viable alternatives and have the designer evaluate their differing predictions for later stages.||校準到單一斷面的模型可能只是參數互相補償，換到新地層或新序列便失準；若只公布最佳誤差不公布多解性，使用者會高估模型的預測能力。~A model calibrated to one section may rely on compensating parameters and fail under a new ground condition or sequence. Reporting only its best error while hiding non-uniqueness encourages overconfidence in predictive capability.||模型曲線完全吻合量測就代表所有參數都是真值。~An exact fit to measured movement means that every fitted parameter is its true value.||反分析文件附參數範圍、相關性和獨立驗證資料，任何用於變更設計的結論須標明仍未辨識項；由模型與設計負責人共同簽認適用情境。~Back-analysis records include parameter ranges, correlations and independent validation. Conclusions used for design changes identify unresolved parameters, and modeling and design leads jointly approve the applicable scenarios.
分層襯砌交接與缺陷圖~Layered-lining handover and defect map||多層襯砌的品質需要逐層追溯，表層完成後會遮蔽接縫、修補與防水介面。缺陷面積比例只能摘要分布，缺陷是否位於力流轉折或滲水路徑比總百分比更影響後續檢查。~Layered lining needs traceability by layer because the final surface hides joints, repairs and waterproofing interfaces. Defect-area fraction summarizes distribution, but whether a defect lies at a load-path change or water route matters more than the overall percentage.||假設檢查面積200 m²、已確認需處置區8 m²，面積比8/200=4%；若其中2 m²位於關鍵接縫，不能被其餘192 m²良好區平均掉。~Assume inspected area 200 m² and confirmed treatment area 8 m²: the fraction is 8/200=4%. If 2 m² lies at critical joints, the 192 m² of satisfactory area cannot average that issue away.||以坐標化照片、厚度點和修補批次建立逐層缺陷圖，抽查下一層施工前的停點簽認；每項處置需有原因、方法核准和完成證據，不能只交總合格面積而省略關鍵接縫的未閉合狀態。~Build layer-by-layer defect maps from located photographs, thickness points and repair batches. Audit hold-point approval before the next layer. Each treatment needs a cause, approved method and completion evidence; total accepted area cannot conceal unresolved conditions at critical joints.||覆蓋後失去定位資訊會使後續滲漏無法連回原缺陷，維修只能猜測路徑；關鍵區域若被總體低缺陷率掩蓋，耐久與可維修性的問題便會延後暴露。~Losing location information after covering a layer prevents later leaks from being linked to original defects. Repairs then rely on guesses, while a low overall defect rate can hide critical zones and postpone durability and maintainability problems.||缺陷總面積比例很小便不必逐項交接其位置。~A small overall defective-area fraction removes the need to hand over each defect location.||未閉合缺陷與已完成修補分開列帳，保留覆蓋前影像和批准版本；品質、結構與維護代表共同確認可追溯資料後，才完成襯砌交接。~Separate unresolved defects from completed repairs and retain pre-covering images and approval versions. Quality, structural and maintenance representatives confirm the traceable evidence before the lining handover is closed.
''')
 course('b149','台階開挖的拱腳承載、核心保留與仰拱閉合時序~Bench excavation, arch-foot bearing, retained core and invert-closure timing',
 '台階法把上半斷面、下半斷面與仰拱分階段形成，各階段的支承位置和自由邊界都會改變。本課追蹤拱腳承載、保留核心、左右開挖與閉合距離的互相影響，再以幾何、物料、收斂及排水資料進行核對。所有算例服務於辨識荷載轉移與資料限制，不指定實際台階長度、開挖步距或拆除程序。~Bench excavation forms the upper section, lower section and invert in stages, changing support locations and free boundaries along the way. The course follows arch-foot bearing, retained core, left-right excavation and closure distance, checking their interaction through geometry, quantities, convergence and drainage evidence. Calculations identify load transfer and data limitations; they do not prescribe actual bench lengths, excavation increments or removal procedures.',
 '台階並不只是一種出碴方便的幾何安排，而是讓支護在不同時間和支承條件下工作的施工系統。Crossrail二〇一四年公開的設計論文回顧一九九二年Heathrow Express試驗隧道，Stepney Green原作者資料則展示上半斷面、台階和仰拱的分割背景。二〇〇九年FHWA手冊提供土建方法參照。本課使用這些公開脈絡比較施工邊界，並未把任何案例的實際尺寸或開挖許可移植給學員。~A bench is more than a convenient shape for muck removal; it is a system in which support operates at changing times and boundary conditions. Crossrail’s 2014 design paper reviews the 1992 Heathrow Express trial, while the Stepney Green authors describe upper, bench and invert subdivisions. The 2009 FHWA manual provides civil-method context. These public examples frame comparisons of construction boundaries; no actual project dimensions or excavation permissions are transferred to learners.',
 '''上半斷面與反力位置~Upper section and reaction locations||上半支護形成後，拱部需求先傳到當時可用的拱腳與地層；下半部未開挖並不表示它沒有受力。簡化對稱反力只適合展示力平衡，傾斜地層和幾何不對稱都會改變左右分配。~After upper support forms, crown demand reaches the available arch feet and surrounding ground. An unexcavated lower section is still mechanically involved. Symmetric reactions illustrate equilibrium only; inclined strata and asymmetric geometry can alter left-right load sharing.||假設垂直合力W=900 kN且對稱，左右反力各450 kN；若假設分配為60%與40%，則為540及360 kN，總和仍為900 kN。~Assume vertical resultant W=900 kN. Symmetry gives 450 kN at each side. A hypothetical 60/40 split instead gives 540 and 360 kN, still summing to 900 kN.||將拱腳位置、支護形狀與量測變形對到同一斷面，核對左右地層是否支持對稱假設；比較拱腳沉陷與上部收斂的關聯，若反應不對稱，保留偏載情境送設計者審查而非直接取平均。~Map arch-foot locations, support shape and measured movement onto one section. Check whether the ground supports symmetry. Compare foot settlement with upper convergence; if behavior is asymmetric, retain eccentric-load scenarios for designer review rather than replacing them with a mean.||一側拱腳較軟會使支護旋轉或重新分配反力，總位移平均值可能不大但局部彎矩上升；只核對總荷載會忽略支承差異所引起的細部需求。~A softer arch foot may rotate the lining or redistribute reactions. Average movement can remain modest while local bending increases. Checking total load alone therefore misses demands caused by unequal support conditions.||總荷載不變就表示左右拱腳需求一定不變。~An unchanged total load means that demand at each arch foot must also remain unchanged.||每階段圖面標出當時有效支承而非最終支承，偏載假設與量測差異另列；下半開挖前由設計和現場技術負責人確認荷載路徑。~Stage drawings show currently effective supports rather than final ones. List eccentric-load assumptions and observational differences separately; design and site technical leads confirm the load path before lower excavation proceeds.
台階長度與暴露歷程~Bench length and exposure history||上半掌子面到下半支護完成點的距離，代表不同斷面停留於開口狀態的時間歷程。進尺相同但中途停機不同，會形成不同暴露時間，因此台階長度不能單獨替代施工序列和地層時間效應。~The distance from the upper face to completed lower support represents a history of open-section exposure. Equal advance with different shutdown periods produces different exposure times. Bench length alone cannot replace a construction sequence or account for time-dependent ground behavior.||假設兩作業點穩定相距12 m、同步平均推進2 m/day，一斷面等待時間12/2=6 days；加入3天停頓則為9 days，非允許等待期。~Assume two work points remain 12 m apart while advancing at 2 m/day. A section waits 12/2=6 days; a three-day shutdown makes nine days. Neither is an allowable waiting period.||從各斷面的時間戳重建上半、下半與仰拱完成日期，特別保留停機而無進尺的區間；將這份歷程與收斂曲線比較，確認時間與距離效應是否混淆，不能用班平均進尺補掉長時間缺測。~Reconstruct upper, lower and invert completion dates for each section using timestamps, preserving stationary shutdown intervals. Compare this history with convergence and distinguish time from distance effects. Shift-average advance must not be used to fill long gaps in observations.||只追蹤掌子面距離會忽略停機期間的變形累積，長台階與時間相依地層疊加時尤其明顯；資料缺少時間戳便無法回溯何時偏離原假設。~Tracking face distance alone misses movement accumulating during shutdown, particularly when a long bench coincides with time-dependent ground. Without timestamps, investigators cannot reconstruct when conditions departed from the original assumptions.||台階長度維持固定就代表每個斷面的受力歷程相同。~A fixed bench length means that every section experiences an identical loading history.||施工日誌以斷面編號連結日期和地層，不只保存累計公尺數；延長等待或調整台階時序須由核准審查程序評估，不以算例天數作排程許可。~Link dates and ground conditions to section identifiers, not just accumulated meters. Extended waiting or altered bench timing follows the approved review process; classroom durations are not scheduling authorization.
拱腳面積與接觸承壓~Arch-foot area and contact bearing||拱腳把集中反力傳到地層或暫時基座，名義寬度不一定等於有效接觸寬度。接觸不平、偏心與局部軟弱層會改變壓力分布，平均承壓只能作為追問接觸機制的起點。~An arch foot transfers concentrated reaction to ground or a temporary base, and nominal width may differ from effective contact. Uneven seating, eccentricity and weak seams alter pressure distribution. Mean bearing is only the starting point for examining that mechanism.||假設反力R=600 kN、有效接觸A=1.2 m²，平均q=500 kPa；若接觸降為0.8 m²，q=750 kPa，未檢查地層承載或沉陷。~Assume reaction R=600 kN and effective contact A=1.2 m². Mean bearing q=500 kPa; with A=0.8 m² it becomes 750 kPa, without checking ground capacity or settlement.||核對竣工接觸尺寸、地層描述及拱腳沉陷，將偏心與接觸缺口畫在同一圖上；必要試驗須代表實際材料和受力方向，不能把其他位置的承載數字直接移用，異常由基礎與支護設計者審查。~Check as-built contact dimensions, ground descriptions and arch-foot settlement, mapping eccentricity and gaps together. Supporting tests must represent the actual material and loading direction. Do not transplant a capacity value from another location; foundation and support designers review anomalies.||基座局部沖刷或軟化使有效面積縮小，支護可能在總反力不變時產生額外沉陷；若外觀遮蔽接觸面，僅看上部襯砌會延後發現承載路徑的變化。~Local erosion or softening can reduce effective footing contact and cause settlement at unchanged total reaction. When the contact is hidden, inspecting only the upper lining delays recognition of the changed bearing path below it.||名義拱腳寬度乘長度永遠等於有效接觸面積。~Nominal arch-foot width multiplied by length always equals the effective loaded contact area.||拱腳交接記錄包含接觸條件和地下水變化，未知面積以範圍呈現；支承處置由設計者核准，平均承壓計算不作現場加載依據。~Arch-foot handover records include contact conditions and groundwater changes, expressing uncertain area as a range. The designer approves support treatment; average-pressure calculations do not authorize field loading.
保留核心與幾何邊界~Retained core and geometric boundaries||保留核心可改變開挖面的幾何與約束，但其力學作用取決於材料連續性、含水和與周圍地層的連接。體積占比只是幾何指標，不能直接換算成支護力或穩定儲備。~A retained core changes excavation geometry and restraint, but its mechanical contribution depends on continuity, water and connection to surrounding ground. Its volume fraction is a geometric indicator rather than a direct measure of support force or stability reserve.||假設整段面積60 m²、長4 m，總體積240 m³；保留核心面積12 m²同長，體積48 m³，占20%，未代表提供20%抗力。~Assume total area 60 m² over 4 m, giving 240 m³. A retained core of 12 m² over the same length occupies 48 m³ or 20%, which does not mean it supplies 20% resistance.||將核心實際輪廓、裂隙及含水狀態與階段圖比對，核對是否有局部先行移除或被設備擾動；若幾何符合而材料明顯改變，仍需重新檢查作用假設，不能只憑剩餘土量宣稱支承有效。~Compare actual core geometry, fractures and moisture with stage drawings. Check for premature local removal or equipment disturbance. Even with correct geometry, changed material requires reassessment of its assumed function; retained quantity alone cannot demonstrate effective restraint.||核心受到鬆動或滲水侵蝕而失去連續性，外形仍可能維持；把外觀體積當成有效支護會忽略內部變質，後續移除時的荷載轉移也可能和原模型不同。~A core can lose continuity through disturbance or seepage while retaining its outline. Treating visible volume as effective support misses internal degradation, and the load transfer during later removal may differ from the original model.||核心保留體積比例就是它提供的抗力比例。~The retained core volume percentage equals the percentage of resistance it provides.||核心記錄同時標示形狀與材料狀態，移除前列出替代支承及核准停點；由地工與施工技術主管確認條件，課堂體積比不構成拆除授權。~Core records show both shape and material condition. Before removal, list replacement restraint and the approved hold point. Geotechnical and construction leads confirm conditions; the classroom volume ratio does not authorize removal.
左右下挖與差異沉陷~Asymmetric lower excavation and settlement||左右下半開挖不同步會改變拱腳的支承與變形，差異沉陷可能令上部支護旋轉。小角度幾何能量化姿態差，卻沒有計入襯砌彎曲、地層再分配和接縫變形，需連結結構模型判讀。~Uneven progress on the lower sides changes arch-foot support and movement. Differential settlement can rotate the upper lining. Small-angle geometry quantifies attitude but omits lining bending, ground redistribution and joint deformation, which need structural interpretation.||假設左右拱腳相距6 m、沉陷差4 mm=0.004 m，剛體小轉角θ≈0.004/6=0.000667 rad=0.0382°，並非容許變形值。~Assume feet are 6 m apart with differential settlement 4 mm=0.004 m. Rigid-body small rotation θ≈0.004/6=0.000667 rad=0.0382°, not an allowable deformation.||使用共同穩定基準量測兩側高程與拱頂位置，對齊左右開挖和支護時間；比較剛體轉動預測與實際斷面畸變，若二者不符須檢討彎曲或接縫機制，不把所有差異都視為儀器誤差。~Measure both foot levels and crown position from a common stable reference, aligning left-right excavation and support times. Compare rigid rotation with actual section distortion. Differences require reviewing bending or joint mechanisms rather than assigning all disagreement to instrumentation.||一側拱腳在下挖時先失去原支承，差異沉陷可放大接縫開口；如果報表只保留左右平均值，旋轉和局部變形便被相互抵消而看不見。~If one foot loses its previous support first, differential settlement can enlarge joint openings. A report retaining only the left-right mean cancels the contrast numerically and hides rotation and localized deformation from review.||左右沉陷平均不大就能排除偏轉與接縫問題。~A small average of left and right settlements rules out rotation and joint problems.||量測報表同時呈現左右值、差值與平均值，保留階段圖版本；任何非對稱序列變更須核對暫時支承，由結構與施工負責人共同核准。~Monitoring reports show left, right, difference and mean values alongside drawing versions. Any asymmetric sequence change requires review of temporary support and joint approval by structural and construction leads.
開挖與出碴質量帳~Excavation and muck mass accounting||台階分部工程量需以相同區間和體積基準對照出碴質量，含水量和密度變化會影響換算。物料帳可發現遺漏區段或超挖線索，但它不能獨立分辨掉塊、密度偏差與稱重誤差。~Bench quantities must match muck mass over the same interval and volume basis. Moisture and density changes influence conversion. Material accounting can flag missing intervals or potential overbreak, but cannot by itself distinguish rock falls, density bias and weighing error.||假設下半面積25 m²、進尺1.5 m、原位密度2400 kg/m³，質量25×1.5×2400=90000 kg=90 t；假設鬆方係數1.4時體積為52.5 m³。~Assume lower area 25 m², advance 1.5 m and in-situ density 2400 kg/m³. Mass is 90000 kg=90 t. With assumed bulking factor 1.4, loose volume is 52.5 m³.||對齊斷面掃描、進尺與車次稱重，單獨扣列可辨識的其他物料及水分變化；檢查資料是否跨越上下台階混裝，未能分離時應標明估計範圍，不能用調整密度的方式強迫帳目相等。~Align section scans, advance and vehicle weights, separately accounting for identifiable other material and moisture changes. Check whether upper and lower muck was mixed. If separation is impossible, state an estimated range instead of adjusting density until the accounts agree.||混裝車次被重複計入上下台階，會誤報超挖並影響地層判讀；反之把未知差額當成密度變化扣掉，可能掩蓋真實輪廓超出和局部掉落。~Counting a mixed vehicle in both upper and lower records falsely reports overbreak and distorts ground interpretation. Conversely, assigning every unexplained difference to density may hide genuine profile excess and localized ground loss.||出碴重量和幾何量不符時，只要修改密度就能解決。~Whenever muck mass and geometry disagree, changing the assumed density resolves the problem.||保留原始稱重與分部歸屬，未解差額由測量、地質和運輸人員共同追查；工程量結算與穩定判斷分開，避免為配平帳目而移除異常證據。~Retain original weights and subdivision assignments. Survey, geological and transport staff jointly investigate unresolved differences, separating quantity settlement from stability assessment so accounting adjustments do not erase anomaly evidence.
閉合追趕與相對速度~Closure catch-up and relative speed||仰拱若落後上半面，其追趕時間由兩者相對速度決定，不能只用仰拱自身速度除以落後距離。持續推進的上半面同時增加待閉合長度，因此產能與支護時序必須放在同一條里程軸上。~If invert closure trails the upper face, catch-up depends on relative speed rather than closure speed alone. Continued upper advance adds open length at the same time. Production and support sequencing therefore need a shared chainage axis.||假設初始落後20 m，上半前進2 m/day、仰拱完成3 m/day，縮短速度1 m/day，理想追平需20 days；若兩者皆2 m/day則距離不縮小。~Assume an initial 20 m gap, upper advance 2 m/day and invert completion 3 m/day. The gap shrinks at 1 m/day, requiring 20 days ideally; equal 2 m/day speeds never close it.||每天量測上半與仰拱有效完成里程，仰拱須依傳力與品質條件認定完成而非只看外形；以兩條累計曲線之差檢查預測，停機和返工分別註記，不能用計畫速度代替實際可用進度。~Measure upper-face and effectively completed invert chainage daily. Completion requires load-transfer and quality conditions, not shape alone. Check forecasts against the difference between cumulative curves, marking shutdown and rework separately rather than substituting planned speeds for actual progress.||仰拱產能等於上半進尺時，看似每班都有閉合工作但落後距離永不縮小；若把累計完成量當成追趕成效，暴露長度會在報表中被錯誤隱藏。~When invert output matches upper advance, closure work occurs every shift but the gap never narrows. Treating cumulative completion as successful catch-up hides the persistent open length in production reporting.||只要每天施工仰拱，最終一定會追上仍前進的掌子面。~Daily invert construction necessarily catches a face that continues advancing at any speed.||進度會議保留兩條里程曲線和相對速度，異常落後與品質返工另列；是否調整上半或仰拱節奏由設計與施工主管共同核准。~Progress reviews retain both chainage curves and relative speed, listing abnormal lag and quality rework separately. Design and construction leads jointly authorize any change to upper-face or invert timing.
測量閉合與基準誤差~Survey closure and reference uncertainty||拱頂沉陷與兩側收斂使用不同幾何投影，必須維持可追溯的基準和符號定義。重複測量可降低獨立隨機誤差，但共用基準位移會同時影響全部讀值，不能藉平均消除。~Crown settlement and side convergence use different geometric projections and need traceable references and sign conventions. Repetition can reduce independent random uncertainty, while movement of a shared reference biases every observation and cannot be removed by averaging.||假設四次獨立讀值各標準差1 mm，平均標準差1/√4=0.5 mm；若另有共用基準偏差2 mm，它仍為2 mm，不隨四次平均消失。~Assume four independent readings each with standard deviation 1 mm. Their mean has 1/√4=0.5 mm standard deviation. A shared 2 mm reference bias remains 2 mm despite averaging.||以區外穩定控制點和閉合測量檢查基準，保存原始高程、儀器設站與時間；將獨立誤差和共同偏差分開列示，若多點同步跳變先查基準，再比較施工事件，不以刪除同日全部資料處理異常。~Use stable external control and closure measurements to check references, retaining original elevations, setups and times. Report independent uncertainty separately from common bias. If many points jump together, investigate the reference before comparing construction events; deleting the entire day is not a diagnosis.||基準點在施工影響區內緩慢下沉，所有量測會低估真實沉陷而仍保持良好重複性；僅以標準差很小判定資料可靠，會錯把精密度當成正確度。~A reference slowly settling inside the construction influence zone makes every observation understate true movement while remaining repeatable. A small standard deviation alone can therefore confuse measurement precision with accuracy and conceal systematic error.||多量幾次取平均就能消除任何種類的測量誤差。~Repeating measurements and averaging removes every type of measurement error, including systematic bias.||監測交接含基準穩定證據及修正版本，任何整體位移修正需測量主管簽認；設計者使用數據前確認共同偏差未被重複讀值的精密度掩蓋。~Monitoring handover includes reference-stability evidence and correction versions. The survey lead approves any common-shift correction, and the designer confirms that repeated-reading precision has not concealed shared bias before using the data.
台階排水與滲流邊界~Bench drainage and seepage boundaries||下半開挖可能改變排水出口與水頭差，流量變化不一定等於滲透係數改變。Darcy一維模型要求飽和層流與明確流徑，實際節理集中流及開挖三維效應必須另行辨識。~Lower excavation can change drainage outlets and head differences, so altered flow need not mean altered conductivity. A one-dimensional Darcy model requires saturated laminar flow and a defined path; fracture concentration and three-dimensional excavation effects require separate interpretation.||假設k=0.0001 m/s、A=15 m²、Δh=8 m、L=12 m，Q=kAΔh/L=0.001 m³/s=3.6 m³/h；水頭差減半則Q減半。~Assume k=0.0001 m/s, A=15 m², Δh=8 m and L=12 m. Q=kAΔh/L=0.001 m³/s=3.6 m³/h; halving head difference halves this ideal flow.||將量水、孔壓和出口高程同步記錄，確認開挖後水頭基準是否改變；比較流量與濁度的時間關係，集中裂隙流不能硬塞進均勻介質公式，異常須由水文地工人員檢查流徑與地層損失。~Record discharge, pore pressure and outlet elevation together, checking whether excavation changed the head reference. Compare flow and turbidity histories. Concentrated fracture flow cannot be forced into a homogeneous-medium formula; hydrogeotechnical specialists review anomalous pathways and possible ground loss.||排水出口下移可能增加水力梯度和細料流失，流量上升卻未必出現立即明顯變形；若只看抽排設備能否負荷，地層侵蝕的機制就可能被忽略。~Lowering an outlet can increase hydraulic gradient and fine-particle loss. Flow may rise before visible movement appears. Focusing only on pump capacity can therefore overlook an erosion mechanism affecting the ground and support beneath the bench.||只要排水設備足夠大，增加湧水就不需要地工判讀。~Sufficient pumping capacity makes additional inflow irrelevant to geotechnical interpretation and support review.||交接排水路徑、孔壓趨勢和濁度異常，不只交泵浦運轉時數；任何改變水頭邊界的方案由水文與支護設計者核准，課堂流量不作抽排設定。~Hand over drainage paths, pressure trends and turbidity anomalies rather than pump hours alone. Hydraulic and support designers approve changes to head boundaries; the classroom discharge is not a pumping setting.
閉合後淨空與驗收餘量~Post-closure clearance and acceptance allowance||襯砌變形、厚度與量測不確定度共同影響可交付淨空，名義設計線不等於竣工可用界面。淨空餘量計算必須使用同一坐標與方向，並保留未來允許變形和設備安裝需求的獨立項目。~Deformation, lining thickness and measurement uncertainty jointly determine deliverable clearance. A nominal design line is not the as-built usable interface. Allowance calculations require common coordinates and directions, with future permitted movement and installation needs listed separately.||假設實測高度5.20 m、所需高度5.05 m、保守量測扣減0.03 m，剩餘餘量5.20-5.05-0.03=0.12 m；未含未來變形預留。~Assume measured height 5.20 m, required height 5.05 m and conservative measurement deduction 0.03 m. Remaining allowance is 0.12 m, before reserving future movement.||用同一坐標系的全斷面掃描檢查最小距離，確認局部凸出、排水和設備支架皆納入；將量測扣減與設計變形預留分開，剩餘餘量不足時送界面設計審查，不能以斷面平均高度代替最不利點。~Check minimum distances using full-section scans in a common coordinate system, including local protrusions, drainage and equipment brackets. Separate measurement deductions from design movement reserves. Inadequate remaining allowance needs interface review; mean section height cannot replace the adverse point.||局部噴層增厚或支架突出會侵入淨空，即使平均斷面符合也可能影響設備安裝；若交接前只檢查中心線高度，側牆與角隅的介面衝突可能延後才被發現。~Local thickening or brackets can intrude into clearance despite acceptable average dimensions. Checking only centerline height before handover leaves sidewall and corner conflicts to emerge later during equipment installation or maintenance planning.||平均斷面尺寸合格就表示所有淨空介面都合格。~Acceptable average section dimensions guarantee that every clearance interface is acceptable.||將最不利點、坐標基準和扣減項目一併交接，保存掃描原檔；土建、設備及維護代表共同確認淨空責任界面後完成驗收。~Hand over adverse locations, coordinate references and deductions together with original scans. Civil, equipment and maintenance representatives jointly confirm responsibility for clearance interfaces before acceptance is completed.
''')
 course('b150','雙側導坑的暫時中隔牆、非對稱受力與拆除荷載轉移~Temporary walls, asymmetry and removal load transfer in side-drift excavation',
 '大斷面側導坑把開挖空間分割成較小區域，但暫時中隔牆及其連接會形成施工期特有的受力系統。本課比較跨度、偏載、牆體剛度與拆除前後的荷載分配，再用測量誤差、階段模型與防水交接檢查推論。課堂的梁、彈簧和壓力算例均不提供拆牆順序或安全許可，學員需辨識何種證據必須由設計者核准。~Side drifts divide a large excavation into smaller regions, while temporary walls and their connections create a construction-specific structural system. This course compares spans, eccentric loading, wall stiffness and load sharing before and after removal, then checks interpretations through survey uncertainty, staged models and waterproofing handover. Beam, spring and pressure examples prescribe neither a removal sequence nor permission; learners identify evidence requiring designer approval.',
 'Stepney Green原作者在二〇一四年公開側壁導坑與襯砌表現的研究，可用來辨識暫時構件如何改變大型地下斷面的分析。另一篇Crossrail設計論文回顧一九九二年Heathrow Express試驗背景，二〇〇九年FHWA手冊則提供土建參考。這些資料顯示施工序列需與地層互制一起考慮；本課特別把側導坑形成期間、中央區開挖與中隔牆移除視為不同結構狀態，不把完工模型倒套所有階段。~The Stepney Green authors published their side-drift and lining-performance study in 2014, providing a context for how temporary members change large-section analysis. A companion Crossrail paper reviews the 1992 Heathrow Express trial, and the 2009 FHWA manual supplies civil context. These references place construction sequence alongside ground interaction. This course treats side-drift formation, central excavation and wall removal as distinct structural states instead of applying the completed-system model retrospectively to every stage.',
 '''分割跨度與梁式比較~Subdivided span and beam comparison||側導坑降低某些施工階段的開放跨度，同時引入暫時支承和接縫。簡支梁均布荷載可展示跨度平方對彎矩的影響，但真實洞室的三維拱效應與地層互制不能由這個比例直接取代。~Side drifts reduce certain open spans while introducing temporary supports and joints. A uniformly loaded simple beam illustrates the squared dependence of moment on span, but the ratio does not replace three-dimensional arching or ground interaction in an actual cavern.||假設q=30 kN/m、L=8 m，M=qL²/8=240 kN·m；將理想跨度減為4 m則M=60 kN·m，僅適用相同均布與簡支邊界。~Assume q=30 kN/m and L=8 m. M=qL²/8=240 kN·m; an ideal 4 m span gives 60 kN·m, under the same uniform loading and simple-support boundaries only.||將每個施工階段的實際開放範圍與暫時牆位置畫出，檢查支承是否已具備傳力能力；若荷載與支承同時改變，必須重新分析而非只套跨度平方比，由洞室設計者審查模型適用性。~Draw the actual open region and temporary-wall position at each stage, checking whether the support can already transfer load. When loading and support change together, reanalyze instead of using the squared-span ratio alone; the cavern designer reviews model applicability.||暫時支承未有效連接而被當成簡支點，會把計算跨度縮得過小並低估彎矩；完工斷面看似合理也不能補救施工期支承假設的缺口。~Treating an unconnected temporary member as an effective simple support artificially shortens the calculated span and understates moment. A plausible completed section does not repair that missing support assumption during construction.||跨度減半就代表整個地下工程的風險必然減為四分之一。~Halving a span necessarily reduces the risk of the whole underground work to one quarter.||階段圖註明每個支點的完成與驗證條件，沒有證據的支承不可默認有效；任何分割變更交由設計者核准，梁式比例只用於敏感度說明。~Stage drawings state completion and verification conditions for every support. Unsupported assumptions cannot count as effective restraints. The designer approves subdivision changes; the beam ratio is only a sensitivity illustration.
左右偏載與合力位置~Left-right loading and resultant position||左右導坑進度或地層不同，可能使合力偏離整體中心並產生額外力矩。將荷載乘其力臂可定位合力，卻不代表襯砌各點反力已知；暫時牆和外環的剛度仍控制內力分配。~Different side-drift progress or ground conditions can shift the resultant away from the section center, creating additional moment. Force times lever arm locates the resultant but does not determine every lining reaction; wall and outer-ring stiffness still control distribution.||假設截面寬12 m，向下力600 kN位於x=2 m、400 kN位於x=10 m，合力位置x=(600×2+400×10)/1000=5.2 m，偏中心0.8 m。~Assume a 12 m section with downward forces 600 kN at x=2 m and 400 kN at x=10 m. Resultant x=(600×2+400×10)/1000=5.2 m, 0.8 m from center.||以一致坐標標出左右地層、施工進度與量測反應，確認合力方向和力臂定義；對比偏載情境的預測與拱頂側移，不可用總沉陷較小消除偏載疑慮，需結構與地工人員共同判斷。~Use common coordinates for left-right ground, construction progress and measured response, checking force directions and lever arms. Compare eccentric-load predictions with crown lateral movement. Modest total settlement does not eliminate eccentricity concerns; structural and geotechnical reviewers interpret them jointly.||左右資料被分開存檔或時間錯位，會將真實非對稱誤看成兩組正常反應；因此中隔牆的側向需求和外環偏心可能未在施工期模型中被捕捉。~Separately stored or mistimed left-right records can make genuine asymmetry look like two normal responses. Temporary-wall lateral demand and outer-ring eccentricity may then be absent from the construction-stage interpretation.||左右總荷載加總正確就不必檢查合力的位置。~Correctly adding the left and right forces removes the need to check resultant location.||左右觀測採共同時鐘與坐標，報告保留合力和偏心而非只有總量；不對稱施工變更須連同暫時牆受力送設計審查。~Use a common clock and coordinates for both sides, reporting resultant and eccentricity rather than total load alone. An asymmetric construction change goes to design review together with its implications for temporary-wall forces.
暫時牆細長與理想屈曲~Temporary-wall slenderness and ideal buckling||暫時牆受壓時的穩定性取決於有效高度、側向拘束與材料剛度，不只取決於壓應力。Euler式只描述理想直桿的彈性屈曲，可用來看高度敏感度，不能當作有裂縫噴凝土牆的完整容量。~Temporary-wall stability depends on effective height, lateral restraint and stiffness, not compressive stress alone. Euler's relation describes ideal elastic buckling of a straight member and illustrates height sensitivity; it is not the complete capacity of a cracked sprayed-concrete wall.||假設兩端鉸接、EI=20000 kN·m²、有效H=6 m，Pcr=π²EI/H²=5483 kN；H增至9 m則2437 kN，未含初始缺陷或非彈性。~Assume pinned ends, EI=20000 kN·m² and effective H=6 m. Pcr=π²EI/H²=5483 kN; at H=9 m it is 2437 kN, excluding imperfections and inelastic behavior.||核對牆高、側向接點和竣工垂直度，檢查接點是否能提供模型假定的拘束；將裂縫及早齡材料資料加入評估，若有效高度有爭議應呈現多種邊界，而非只選得到最大容量的一組。~Check wall height, lateral connections and as-built verticality, verifying that connections supply assumed restraint. Include cracking and early-age material evidence. When effective height is uncertain, show multiple boundaries rather than choosing only the one producing the largest capacity.||一個側向接點尚未成形或先被解除，會增加有效長度而降低穩定性；即使平均壓應力不變，牆體仍可能出現側彎與二階效應，不能靠壓應力檢核排除。~A lateral connection that is unfinished or released early increases effective length and reduces stability. Mean compression may remain unchanged while lateral bending and second-order effects develop, so a stress-only check cannot exclude the problem.||暫時牆壓應力低於材料強度就不會發生失穩。~A temporary wall cannot become unstable while compressive stress remains below material strength.||接點狀態列入每階段核查表，任何拘束改變由暫時工程設計者審查；課堂Euler數值僅示範尺度，不能作拆除接點或加載依據。~Include connection status in each stage checklist and refer every restraint change to the temporary-works designer. Classroom Euler values illustrate scale; they do not authorize removal of a connection or additional loading.
中隔牆偏心與拉壓邊緣~Wall eccentricity and edge stresses||軸力偏離中隔牆中心會產生彎矩，兩側邊緣可能一側壓縮一側受拉。線彈性未裂截面可揭示平均值掩蓋的差異，但開裂後必須重新檢討有效剛度與力流，不可直接延用同一分布。~An axial force offset from the temporary-wall center creates bending, potentially compressing one edge and tensioning the other. An uncracked elastic section exposes differences hidden by the mean. Once cracking occurs, effective stiffness and load transfer need reassessment rather than unchanged extrapolation.||假設單位寬N=500 kN、e=0.10 m、t=0.30 m，M=50 kN·m；σ=N/t±6M/t²=1.667±3.333 MPa，兩緣5與-1.667 MPa。~For a 1 m strip assume N=500 kN, eccentricity e=0.10 m and thickness t=0.30 m. M=50 kN·m; σ=N/t±6M/t²=1.667±3.333 MPa, giving 5 and -1.667 MPa at the edges.||以實測牆體輪廓、接點偏移與裂縫圖核對偏心方向，兩側應變需扣除溫度與初始讀值差；若拉側反應顯著，應檢查開裂模型和連接條件，不把單側感測值代表整個牆截面。~Use measured wall profiles, connection offsets and crack maps to check eccentricity direction. Correct opposite-side strains for temperature and initial offsets. Significant tensile response requires checking cracking and connections; one sensor cannot represent the full wall section.||施工偏差把力流推向牆邊，可能在名義平均壓力可接受時造成拉裂與局部壓碎；如果只量一側，還可能把彎曲誤判為均勻軸向受力。~Construction deviation may move the load path toward an edge, producing tension or crushing despite a modest nominal mean. Measuring only one side can further misclassify bending as uniform axial loading across the section.||中隔牆只承擔軸向壓力，所以不需要考慮偏心彎矩。~A temporary dividing wall carries axial compression only, so eccentric bending need not be considered.||交接同時保存牆厚、偏心來源和兩側量測，不將平均應力替代邊緣檢查；異常裂縫由暫時工程與襯砌設計者共同評估。~Retain wall thickness, eccentricity sources and observations on both sides at handover. Mean stress does not replace edge checks; temporary-works and lining designers jointly assess anomalous cracking.
支承剛度與荷載重分配~Support stiffness and load redistribution||中央區形成後，不同支承可共同承載；在理想剛性橫梁下，各支承分得的荷載與剛度成比例。移除其中一項會改變位移和剩餘需求，即使外荷載不變，也不能沿用拆除前的內力。~After the central region forms, supports may share load. Under an ideal rigid cross-member their shares are proportional to stiffness. Removing one changes displacement and remaining demand even at unchanged external load, so pre-removal internal forces cannot simply be retained.||假設總F=1000 kN、並聯k1=20及k2=30 kN/mm，位移20 mm、分力400與600 kN；移除k1後位移1000/30=33.33 mm。~Assume total F=1000 kN and parallel stiffnesses k1=20 and k2=30 kN/mm. Displacement is 20 mm and forces are 400 and 600 kN. Removing k1 gives 1000/30=33.33 mm.||核對模型是否真能視為共同位移的並聯支承，再比較移除前後的位移和內力資料；材料齡期、接縫與地層接觸改變須分別建模，不能只把被移除構件從圖上刪去而保持其他內力不變。~Check whether shared displacement really supports a parallel-spring idealization, then compare pre- and post-change movements and force evidence. Model material age, joints and changed ground contact separately. Erasing a removed member from the drawing while retaining all other forces is not analysis.||剩餘支承較柔或已有損傷，重新分配後的位移可能比原預測大，並引發額外偏心；若只確認被拆牆本身可移除，會漏掉承接荷載的系統需求。~If the remaining support is flexible or damaged, redistribution can produce greater movement and additional eccentricity than expected. Checking only that the wall itself can be removed misses the demands on the system taking over its load.||外荷載不變就表示拆除一個支承後其他構件內力不變。~Unchanged external loading means that removing one support cannot change forces in the others.||拆除審查須指明由誰承接每個力分量，附替代系統的齡期與驗證證據；設計者核准後才有正式程序，本課彈簧例不提供拆除順序。~A removal review identifies the recipient of each force component and includes age and verification evidence for the replacement system. Formal procedures follow designer approval; this spring example specifies no removal sequence.
暫時構件減少與需求缺口~Temporary-member reduction and demand gap||受力構件數量減少時，總可用抗力與個別需求都可能改變；將額定值簡單相加只是一個理想上限，實際分配受剛度、偏心及連接控制。即使這個理想上限不足，也不應靠平均分攤掩蓋缺口。~Reducing load-carrying members can change both available resistance and individual demand. Adding nominal values is only an ideal upper bound because stiffness, eccentricity and connections govern distribution. If even that upper bound is insufficient, averaging cannot remove the gap.||假設四個獨立同向支承各有200 kN已給定能力，總800 kN；少一個後僅600 kN，對假設需求700 kN差100 kN，未含分項與群體效應。~Assume four independent supports with supplied same-direction resistance 200 kN each, totaling 800 kN. With one absent, 600 kN remains against assumed demand 700 kN, leaving a 100 kN gap before factors or group effects.||建立每階段支承清單與方向圖，核對能力是否有可追溯設計依據以及構件是否實際有效；先查總量平衡，再查個別分配和連接，任何需求缺口須由設計者明確處理，不能靠修改報表平均值消失。~Build stage-specific support inventories and force-direction diagrams, checking traceable resistance assumptions and actual availability. Review total equilibrium before individual distribution and connections. The designer must explicitly address any demand gap; changing an average in a report cannot remove it.||若構件尚未達齡期或接點未完成卻被算入可用數量，能力表會高估實際系統；逐項少算需求又可能讓總表看似平衡，掩蓋某一關鍵施工階段的缺口。~Counting members before adequate age or connection completion overstates the available system. Understating separate demands can then make the totals appear balanced while concealing a gap at a critical construction stage.||只要平均分到各支承的力不大，缺少構件就沒有影響。~Missing members have no effect as long as the average force per support looks modest.||構件清單分開列已完成、已驗證與待核准狀態，禁止把計畫構件當成現有支承；暫時工程主管和結構設計者共同簽認每階段力流。~Distinguish completed, verified and pending members in the inventory. Planned members cannot count as existing support. The temporary-works lead and structural designer jointly approve the load path at each stage.
共同基準與相關誤差~Shared reference and correlated uncertainty||左右導坑量測常共用基準，因此誤差可能相關；平方和只適用獨立分量。若要比較組合量，必須依加減方向包含共變異數，不然資料看似精密也可能低估或高估實際不確定度。~Measurements in both drifts may share a reference, creating correlated errors. Root-sum-square applies only to independent components. For a combined quantity, covariance must follow the chosen addition or subtraction; otherwise apparent precision can understate or overstate uncertainty.||假設相加量兩項標準差2與3 mm、相關係數ρ=0.5，σ=√(2²+3²+2×0.5×2×3)=4.36 mm；若獨立則3.61 mm。~For a sum, assume standard deviations 2 and 3 mm and correlation ρ=0.5. σ=√(2²+3²+2×0.5×2×3)=4.36 mm; independence would give 3.61 mm.||核對兩組量測是否共用設站、控制點或氣象修正，先定義比較量是和還是差；從重複觀測估計相關性時保留樣本限制，基準偏差另行調查，不以套入相關係數掩蓋未查明的系統誤差。~Check shared setup, control and atmospheric correction, first defining whether the comparison is a sum or difference. Retain sample limitations when estimating correlation from repetitions. Investigate reference bias separately rather than inserting a coefficient to conceal an unexplained systematic error.||把共用基準的資料當完全獨立會錯估合成不確定度，導致異常判定過度敏感或不夠敏感；若正負號也混淆，左右差異甚至可能被錯誤放大。~Treating shared-reference data as independent misstates combined uncertainty and can make anomaly detection too sensitive or too insensitive. Confusing signs adds another error and may exaggerate a left-right difference that the observations do not support.||任何兩項量測不確定度都可直接平方和開根號。~Any two measurement uncertainties can always be combined by root-sum-square without further checks.||量測報告保留坐標、組合公式與共用誤差來源，相關性不明時提供情境範圍；監測主管與設計者確認後，才用於施工階段比較。~Reports retain coordinates, combination formulas and shared-error sources. Where correlation is unknown, provide scenario bounds. Monitoring and design leads confirm the treatment before using it to compare construction stages.
階段模型與保留驗證~Staged model and withheld validation||階段模型必須依實際完成狀態啟用構件，才有可能對照量測；總誤差很小不代表每個階段都合理。保留未用於校準的觀測能檢查外推能力，殘差的時間方向比單一誤差數字更有資訊。~A staged model activates members according to actual completion before it can be compared with observations. Small total error does not make every stage credible. Withheld observations test predictive performance, and the temporal pattern of residuals often matters more than one summary metric.||假設三個保留觀測為4、7、10 mm，預測為5、7、8 mm，誤差為1、0、-2 mm，RMSE=√[(1²+0²+2²)/3]=1.29 mm。~Assume withheld observations 4, 7 and 10 mm with predictions 5, 7 and 8 mm. Errors are 1, 0 and -2 mm; RMSE=√[(1²+0²+2²)/3]=1.29 mm.||檢查校準與驗證資料是否真正分離，將殘差對照中隔牆狀態與開挖時序；若後期持續低估，須檢討構件啟用、剛度及荷載邊界，不能只用全期RMSE較小便宣稱下一階段已驗證。~Verify that calibration and validation data are separate, comparing residuals with wall status and excavation chronology. Persistent late underprediction requires reviewing member activation, stiffness and load boundaries. A small whole-history RMSE does not validate the next stage automatically.||把驗證資料回填校準後再稱為獨立驗證，會製造過度樂觀的準確度；模型在拆除後系統性低估時，平均誤差可能仍被前期良好吻合稀釋。~Reusing validation observations for calibration and still calling them independent creates optimistic accuracy. Systematic underprediction after removal can also be diluted by good early fits when only a whole-history average is reported.||模型全期平均誤差很小便表示每一次構件變更都可靠。~A small whole-history average error makes every modeled member change reliable and validated.||模型版本記錄每個構件的啟用日期與校準資料集，保留後期驗證不回填；拆除相關預測與實際差異由模型和暫時工程負責人共同審查。~Model versions record activation dates and calibration datasets, keeping later validation genuinely separate. Modeling and temporary-works leads jointly review differences between removal-related predictions and observations.
拆牆介面與水壓路徑~Wall-removal interfaces and water-pressure paths||中隔牆移除後，原接觸和施工縫會成為必須確認的防水介面；外部水頭不會因牆被拆除而消失。局部平面水壓合力可顯示需求尺度，但接縫滲漏與結構傳力要分別驗證。~After a dividing wall is removed, former contacts and construction joints become interfaces requiring waterproofing verification. External head does not disappear with wall removal. A local planar pressure resultant illustrates scale, while leakage paths and structural transfer need separate checks.||假設淡水水頭18 m，p=9.81×18=176.58 kPa；在假設平面面積1.5 m²上F=264.87 kN，未代表整個曲面襯砌的合力。~Assume freshwater head 18 m: p=9.81×18=176.58 kPa. On an ideal plane area 1.5 m², F=264.87 kN; this is not the resultant over the whole curved lining.||將拆牆後暴露的接縫、修補與防水連續性定位記錄，核對外水頭與排水設計是否一致；以核准品質試驗確認介面，乾燥表面不能排除未來水頭增加，需由防水及結構負責人共同核查。~Locate exposed joints, repairs and waterproof continuity after removal, checking consistency between external head and drainage design. Approved quality tests verify interfaces. A dry surface does not exclude future head increase, so waterproofing and structural leads review the conditions together.||拆除留下的凹槽或施工縫若未完成相容處置，可能形成沿界面的滲流路徑；早期沒有漏水不代表耐久可靠，後續水頭改變才可能暴露缺陷。~A recess or construction joint left without compatible treatment can form an interface seepage path. Lack of early leakage does not establish durability, because a later head change may be what exposes the defect.||暫時牆拆掉後，其原接縫就不再影響永久襯砌。~Once a temporary wall is removed, its former joints no longer affect the permanent lining.||防水交接另列原中隔牆介面及修補版本，保留覆蓋前證據與維護定位；未閉合項須由相應設計責任人處理，不以無漏水照片取代核准。~Waterproofing handover identifies former wall interfaces and repair versions, retaining pre-covering evidence and maintenance locations. Responsible designers resolve open items; a photograph without leakage is not a substitute for approval.
施工狀態清單與交接~Construction-state register and handover||大型洞室交接需要知道哪些暫時構件已移除、哪些永久介面已驗證，僅有完工外觀圖會遺失施工歷程。清單完成率是資料管理指標，關鍵未閉合項的風險仍需個別決策。~Cavern handover needs the status of removed temporary members and verified permanent interfaces. An as-finished view alone loses construction history. Register completion is a data-management measure; critical unresolved items still require individual engineering decisions.||假設交接列80項界面，已核准76項，完成率76/80=95%；剩餘4項若含荷載轉移驗證，即使比例只有5%也不能自動結案。~Assume 80 interface items with 76 approved: completion is 76/80=95%. If the remaining four include load-transfer verification, their 5% share does not justify automatic closure.||逐項抽查清單能否連到圖面版本、原始量測與核准記錄，特別檢查拆除前後狀態是否一致；將待辦項依機制和責任分列，不能只交一個總完成百分比，維護單位也須能定位永久介面。~Audit whether each register item links to drawing versions, original observations and approvals, especially consistency before and after removal. Classify open items by mechanism and responsibility rather than handing over one percentage. Maintenance staff must also be able to locate permanent interfaces.||暫時狀態未更新會讓後續人員以為仍有某個支承，或誤認已完成防水修補；這類文件錯誤可能使維護決策建立在不存在的構件或未驗證的介面上。~An outdated temporary-state record can make later staff assume a support remains or a waterproof repair is complete. Maintenance decisions may then rely on a nonexistent member or an interface whose condition has never been verified.||交接完成率夠高就能把所有剩餘項目視為行政細節。~A high completion percentage makes every remaining handover item merely an administrative detail.||保留施工狀態歷程與永久資產清單的對應，未閉合項指定責任人及核准條件；設計、施工、品質和維護代表共同確認後完成交接。~Preserve the link between construction-state history and the permanent asset register, assigning owners and approval conditions to unresolved items. Design, construction, quality and maintenance representatives jointly confirm the record before handover closes.
''')
